local.properties
.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex

# The Play signing keystore. A signing key committed to history cannot be
# cleanly rotated away, and Android identifies an app by its signing key — lose
# it and existing installs can never be updated, only uninstalled and replaced.
# See HANDOFF_REMOTE_MOBILE.md §10.1.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# No exceptions any more. A preview key was committed for a while, deliberately, so
# that consecutive CI builds would install over each other while the repository was
# private and APKs were handed over one at a time. Publishing the repository ended
# that trade: a signing key anyone can read is a signing key anyone can sign with,
# and Android's refusal to install a differently-signed update is the only thing
# standing between a user and a hostile APK. The release key now lives in CI secrets
# and is written to keystore/ at build time. See keystore/README.md.

